In the arrow-shaped polygon shown below, the angles at vertices $A$, $C$, $D$, $E$, and $F$ are right angles, $BC = FG = 5$, $CD = FE = 20$, $DE = 10$, and $AB = AG$.  Find the area of polygon $ABCDEFG$.

[asy]
unitsize(1.5 cm);

pair A, B, C, D, E, F, G;

A = (0,0);
B = (1,1);
C = (1,0.5);
D = (2.5,0.5);
E = (2.5,-0.5);
F = (1,-0.5);
G = (1,-1);

draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--G--cycle);

label("$A$", A, W);
label("$B$", B, NE);
label("$C$", C, S);
label("$D$", D, NE);
label("$E$", E, SE);
label("$F$", F, N);
label("$G$", G, SE);
label("$5$", (B + C)/2, dir(0));
label("$20$", (C + D)/2, N);
label("$10$", (D + E)/2, dir(0));
label("$20$", (E + F)/2, S);
label("$5$", (F + G)/2, dir(0));
[/asy]

